# R1 (docs/monorepo-boundaries.md, "Inside a React package: the component is not
# the coordinator"). Every React module that awaits or chains a promise, with
# exactly how many such sites it has (`await`, `for await`, `.then`/`.catch`/
# `.finally`). `pnpm check:react-coordination` fails on any module missing
# here, and on any count that no longer matches, in either direction.
#
# One entry per line: `<sites> <path>`. A blank line ends a group, and each
# group's `#` lines must include one starting `Coordination:` (why this module
# coordinates async work instead of a runtime outside React doing it) or
# `Grandfathered:`. A new entry, or a raised count, goes in its own group
# under `Coordination:`; it never joins or raises the grandfathered group.
#
# This file is where R1 is reviewed. The check counts; it does not judge.

# Grandfathered: these coordinated before R1 landed. Debt, not a judgment that
# each is fine: a count here may only fall (lower it in the same change), and
# an entry leaves when its module stops awaiting.
